**What the cohort is.** Five commands (`create_session`,
`register_participant`, `record_check_in`, `update_roster_status`,
`change_session_status`) against `archava_attendance`'s six tables, with
the audit-A04 correction as a row-SELECT property (`session_id=$3`) plus a
pure domain policy (`check_in_refusal`) that checks the roster↔session
binding first; seat allocation and check-in serialize on the session/roster
row locks; duplicate roster/ticket/session-code boundaries are 409
(`D23`); `scope=assigned` narrows every read (`D24`); a session window must
strictly advance (`D25`). Six read projections (access, session list,
detail+roster+check-ins, roster, check-in ledger, command status) and
fourteen named witnesses grow the same `P-ERP-R07` proof from 26 to 40.

**Apply:** `patch -p1 --forward --fuzz=0 < PACKET-009.diff` on
main+003…008. The new source files (`domain|adapters|host/src/erp/attendance.rs`,
`host/tests/erp_attendance.rs`, the two `mod.rs` lines, `tools/rust/erp/verify-r07.mjs`
